                <li><b>Terminal 3 - </b>Commuter terminal for smaller inter-island operators</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Agricultural Inspection at HNL</h4>
            <p>All passengers arriving from the mainland must proceed through Hawaii's unique agricultural inspection.</p>
            <p><b>Requirements:</b></p>
            <ul>
                <li>Declaration of all plants, animals, and fresh food items on an agricultural form distributed inflight.</li>
                <li>Strict quarantine laws prohibit most fresh fruits, vegetables, and flowers from entering Hawaii.</li>
                <li>Pets require health certificates and possible quarantine depending on pre-arrival rabies testing</li>
                <li>No passport required for US citizens; standard domestic travel documentation suffices.</li>
            </ul>
            <h4>Transportation from HNL to Central Honolulu</h4>
            <ul>
                <li><b>SpeediShuttle and Roberts Hawaii -</b> Shared shuttle services to Waikiki hotels; cost approximately $15-$18; journey time 30-45 minutes</li>
                <li><b>TheBus (Route 20) -</b> Most economical option; cost approximately $3; journey time 45-60 minutes to Waikiki</li>
                <li><b>Taxi / Uber / Lyft - </b>Typical fares to Waikiki $35-$50; journey time 20-35 minutes depending on H-1 freeway traffic</li>
                <li><b>Rental Car -</b> Essential for exploring North Shore, Windward Coast, and island interior; major agencies at consolidated rental car facility</li>
            </ul>
